00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.700
On the last episode of Dragon Ball Z,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.320
it appeared as though Vegeta had the evil Cell in his inescapable grip.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.780
But don't count the slithering Cell out just yet.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.300
Knowing of the Saiyan's thirst for a challenge,

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:24.120
Cell lured Vegeta into a mind-boggling agreement.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:24.980
You're android.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:29.300
Hopefully the next time we meet, you won't be in such a pathetic state.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.080
It's quite embarrassing.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.530
What did I tell you?

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.890
But will allowing Cell to become complete B-Vegeta's final mistake?

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:44.100
Not Trunks has anything to say about it.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:51.760
Meanwhile, Krillin held the fate of the other androids in the palm of his hands, literally.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.560
With one push of a button, Krillin could shut down Android 18 for good,

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.980
preventing Cell from ever reaching his final heinous...

